cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use a parameter card or a literature comparison, please also cite the original papers listed in the files you use."
type: software
title: "ferroelectric-models: ferroelectric switching and hysteresis models with a Verilog-A multi-domain NLS capacitor model"
abstract: >-
  Python implementations of standard ferroelectric switching and hysteresis
  models (Landau-Khalatnikov, Preisach/FORC, KAI/NLS/Merz, PUND analysis) and a
  dynamic multi-domain nucleation-limited-switching capacitor model for
  HfO2-type thin films, with a Verilog-A version compiled with OpenVAF and
  verified in ngspice against the Python reference. Optional history terms
  describe wake-up, fatigue, logarithmic-time imprint and leakage growth.
authors:
  - alias: Celivem
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Celivem/ferroelectric-models"
url: "https://github.com/Celivem/ferroelectric-models"
keywords:
  - ferroelectric
  - hafnium oxide
  - HZO
  - hysteresis
  - Preisach model
  - nucleation-limited switching
  - compact model
  - Verilog-A
  - ngspice
